Contents: factual metadata only about Christopher Alexander, Sara Ishikawa,
and Murray Silverstein, "A Pattern Language" (Oxford University Press, 1977):
pattern numbers, names, confidence asterisks (as 0/1/2), section and
subsection groupings, and the directed cross-reference structure (1,758
edges after direction resolution). It contains NONE of the book's prose, and
none of the apl-md transcription's prose. Facts are not copyrightable
(Feist v. Rural, 1991; US Copyright Office Circular 33).

The apl-md transcription itself is reproduced by its author with written
permission from patternlanguage.com (2024-04-14, non-commercial with
attribution — see its LICENSE.md). We take no text from it; extraction
fetches the files transiently and writes only the metadata above.

Validation: the extracted metadata was cross-checked against two independent
sources (the BeksOmega/pattern-language-graph GraphML and the
iwritewordsgood.com/apl mirror). Asterisks agree with the mirror on 225/227
parseable patterns; the undirected edge structure agrees at Jaccard 0.93
(differences are single-file declarations, expected). Full log:
data-notes/validation.md.

History: v1 of this pipeline vendored BeksOmega/pattern-language-graph
patterns.graphml (MIT, commit 1404507). Three-source validation showed its
edges (Jaccard 0.34 vs the book mirror) and stars (172/227 agreement) were
